  "body": "Stacked on #2001 (merge #2001 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nStore explicit tap hand on the tool.\nDefault older tools to right-hand.\nRefuse malformed hand values by name.\nPreserve hand through catalog import, tool JSON, project files, tool libraries, editor drafts and undoable commands.\nShow the left-hand choice in the tap editor.\nState that left-hand posting is unavailable.\n\nRefuse left-hand taps in the shared posting preflight before records or NC files are emitted.\nThe refusal names the operation and tool.\nIt covers all eight built-in posts that implement tapping: Fanuc, Haas, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mazak, Tormach PathPilot, Doosan DNM and Fanuc Lathe.\nRight-hand output stays unchanged.\n\nWrite project version 62 for saved projects.\nUse library version 2 only for exports containing a left-hand tap.\nThese versions make older readers refuse the files instead of silently losing hand.\nKeep right-hand-only libraries at version 1.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe tool model had no tap hand.\nThe tool JSON reader silently discarded an unknown hand field.\nA left-hand declaration therefore could not survive the existing data path.\nEvery supported tapping cycle used the right-hand assumption.\n\nEffort: high. No escalation.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll 14 focused pins pass.\nThe first pin failed at runtime on unchanged product code.\nIt read `Null` instead of `left` after the JSON round trip.\n\nApp pins:\n\n- `left_hand_tap_survives_tool_json_roundtrip`\n- `absent_hand_is_legacy_right_and_unknown_hands_are_refused`\n- `every_tapping_post_refuses_left_hand_for_rigid_floating_and_auto`\n- `right_hand_tap_still_posts_on_every_tapping_post`\n- `fanuc_lathe_posts_right_hand_and_refuses_left_hand_axial_taps`\n- `hand_survives_project_and_library_and_old_readers_are_barred`\n- `changing_cached_tap_hand_is_undoable_and_cannot_post_right_hand_cycles`\n\nTool pins:\n\n- `catalog_preserves_left_tap_and_defaults_legacy_tools_to_right`\n- `catalog_refuses_invalid_hands_by_tool_and_field_name`\n\nUI integration pins:\n\n- `tap_tool_draft_preserves_both_hands`\n- `left_hand_tap_add_is_undoable_and_redoable`\n- `changing_tap_hand_roundtrips_through_undo_and_redo`\n\nUI structural pins:\n\n- `tap_hand_checkbox_stages_until_apply_and_undo_restores_right`\n- `a_non_tap_tool_has_no_tap_hand_checkbox`\n\nAll 11 mutation cases failed at runtime and passed after restoration:\n\n- Restore the upstream posting preflight.\n- Restore the upstream tool-library implementation.\n- Accept an invalid hand as right-hand.\n- Revert project version 62 to 61.\n- Drop hand when writing the tool DTO.\n- Drop hand when reading the tool DTO.\n- Drop hand in catalog conversion.\n- Refuse library version 2 in the new reader.\n- Drop hand in `ToolUi::from_tool`.\n- Drop hand in `ToolUi::to_tool`.\n- Ignore the checkbox selection.\n\nThe posting and library replays restored whole files from `upstream/main`.\nThe new enum, DTO, catalog and UI mutations changed the relevant behavior in place.\nAn additional whole-upstream posting-preflight replay also made the Fanuc Lathe pin fail at runtime.\nIt passed after restoration.\nAll mutations were restored.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all five steps with zero failures in 27.4 minutes.\nAll-targets clippy with `-D warnings` passed for `camcraft-app`, `camcraft-tools`, `camcraft-motion`, `camcraft-ui` and `camcraft-post`.\nThe final Fanuc Lathe coverage required no product-code change.\nAll seven app pins and app all-targets clippy passed again after that test was added.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical control ran the output.\nThe full batch and release snapshot lanes were not run.\nThis change refuses left-hand posting; it does not implement left-hand controller cycles.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2001 changes shared conversion functions, including `ToolUi::from_tool`, the `ToolDto` conversions, the catalog definition conversion and `tool_editor_window`.\nThis branch started from #2001 at `028a0ad0` over upstream/main `cda3d589`.\n\n- #2000, #1798 and #1330 each touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. They share `crates/ui/src/state.rs`.\n- #1931, #1717 and #1209 each touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. They share `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs`.\n- #1817 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. It changes other declarations in `crates/app/src/project/mod.rs` and another test in `crates/app/tests/operations.rs`.\n- #1713 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. It changes other functions in `crates/motion/tests/center_cut_owed.rs`, `crates/app/tests/operations.rs` and `crates/app/tests/golden_cl.rs`.\n\nChangelog: Store tap handedness and refuse unsupported left-hand taps before posting.\n\nFixes #1453\n\n\n## Review fixes\n\nCommit `83dfc4d7` records the breaking file compatibility change with a `fix(project)!:` marker and a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer. Saved projects use format 62. Older readers refuse them so they cannot silently lose tap hand. The version barrier remains in place.\n\n## UI evidence\n\nThe tap editor images render the actual editor. Before uses parent `028a0ad0`'s `pages.rs`, which has no hand control. After uses the reviewed UI. The new checkbox offers left-hand taps and states that posting is unavailable.\n\nThe waterjet images are the existing evidence from parent #2001, which remains part of this PR. All images are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch. Links pin the image commits.\n\n| Control | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tap hand | ![Tap editor before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0505991090a12d79ca7c575847b61aaed16783f0/2026/tap-hand-before.png) | ![Tap editor after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0505991090a12d79ca7c575847b61aaed16783f0/2026/tap-hand-after.png) |\n| Waterjet tool choice | ![Waterjet tool choice before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2d4e8ca80b70aa0adb77e545c60f89a583dbaf8e/2001/tool-choice-before.png) | ![Waterjet tool choice after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2d4e8ca80b70aa0adb77e545c60f89a583dbaf8e/2001/tool-choice-after.png) |\n| Waterjet machine choice | ![Waterjet machine choice before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2d4e8ca80b70aa0adb77e545c60f89a583dbaf8e/2001/machine-choice-before.png) | ![Waterjet machine choice after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2d4e8ca80b70aa0adb77e545c60f89a583dbaf8e/2001/machine-choice-after.png) |\n\nThe waterjet recipe editor shows material, plate thickness, kerf and pierce values:\n\n![Waterjet recipe after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2d4e8ca80b70aa0adb77e545c60f89a583dbaf8e/2001/recipe-valid-after.png)\n",
